<header><p class="enc-kicker">Religion / idea · deity</p><h1 class="enc-title">Osiris</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Osiris was the ancient Egyptian god of the dead, the afterlife and regeneration, shown as a mummified king. In myth he was murdered by his brother <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/seth">Seth</a> and revived by his wife <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/isis">Isis</a>, becoming the father of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/horus">Horus</a> and ruler of the underworld. Abydos was his chief cult centre, and from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/middle-francia">Middle Kingdom</a> pilgrims and officials set up memorials along the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/processional-way">processional way</a> to his supposed tomb there.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/osiris.jpg" alt="Osiris" width="320" height="695" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Jeff Dahl · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Standing_Osiris.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
